alex: FYI hitting a weird fncall return shape in sample-app tests — when the model emits two top-level objects we end up with an array and our fncall helper chokes. repro below.
```
// expecting a single object per function call
// function signature: createUser -> { user: {...}, metadata: {...} }
// model streaming output (chunks):
{"user":{"id":1,"name":"alice"}}
{"metadata":{"env":"prod"}}
// client currently collects chunks and naive-assembles them into an array:
[ {user...}, {metadata...} ]
// fncall helper assumes top-level object -> throws on access like payload.user
```

priya: Ugh, saw this before. JSON mode + streaming can split root objects; sometimes we get multiple top-level JSON values which becomes an array. SDK normalization fixed many cases but fncall path missed it.

jonah: Can you paste exact client logs/headers? Are you using `jsonMode: true` or streaming over SSE?

alex: Logs:
```
RESPONSE_CHUNKS:
{"user":{"id":1,"name":"alice"}}
{"metadata":{"env":"prod"}}
```
Client collects chunks and ends up doing `[` + chunks.join(',') + `]` to assemble when it thinks there are multiple root values. Then the fncall parser does `JSON.parse(...)` and checks `typeof parsed === 'object' && !Array.isArray(parsed)` which fails.

mei: Ah — streaming split object boundaries is expected. Quick options: 1) change function return shape to always wrap in an envelope (e.g., `{payload: {...}}`) — breaking for users. 2) SDK helper: add a fallback that if fncall expects object but parsed is array of objects, try to merge array elements into one object (later keys overwrite earlier). 3) add a `jsonMode: 'strict' | 'lenient'` flag so evals/CI can opt-in to strict parsing.

rob: We shouldn't force schema changes on integrators. Fallback behavior in SDK makes sense but must be opt-in or limited. Suggest default: attempt merge, log warning, and respect `jsonMode: 'strict'` to error out.

priya: I'll prototype a small change in the JS helper: detect `Array.isArray(parsed) && parsed.every(isPlainObject)` -> `Object.assign({}, ...parsed)` and then continue fncall flow. If strict, throw instead. Will add unit tests for chunked streams.

alex: That sounds good. Note: this also breaks TS typings because return type becomes `unknown[]` in some paths; PR should keep typedef as expected object and only widen if strict flag is on.

devex-bot: Created ticket INF-4321: "fncall: support array->object fallback for streaming multi-chunk outputs" and linked sample-app failing test.

jonah: Add a unit test that simulates a chunked stream which yields two top-level JSON values; CI flake we've been seeing likely comes from this exact pattern.

mei: Docs note: explain `jsonMode` flavors and streaming caveats. Recommend sample-app default to `jsonMode: 'lenient'` for onboarding but `strict` in evals and production rollouts.

alex: Thanks — @priya ping me when the PR is up, I'll run it through the matrix of node/browser/runtime configs.

priya: Will do, aiming for a small patch + tests today. :thumbsup:
